data: {"type":"response.function_call_arguments.done","sequence_number":583,"item_id":"fc_00227d6e6d82ad62016adb1b92da3c8191981863884d2d6682","output_index":1,"arguments":"{\"obstacle_json\":\"{\\\"status\\\":\\\"SOURCE_UNAVAILABLE\\\",\\\"location\\\":\\\"Pinned Mathlib source registration for the Hausdorff-dimension facts required by proof-draft.json (including hausdorffMeasure_of_lt_dimH and hausdorffMeasure_of_dimH_lt), and consequently completion of the requested NL0 source graph\\\",\\\"explanation\\\":\\\"The declared library tools are not fully operational in this stage case. search_mathlib and read_mathlib did locate and display Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean; its displayed lines 114–135 contain the relevant theorem statements. However, the explicitly required probe_library calls for both declarations were rejected before probing with `sandbox-exec: ... test/results/geometry-nl0-v1/stage/case/library/M001-0001/work/sandbox.sb: No such file or directory` (and likewise for M002). Thus no checked M-source evidence or full probed signatures/axiom reports can be registered. I cannot fabricate the required evidence or submit an NL0 falsely claiming source completion. This is an operational source-evidence block, not a finding that the exercise is false or that the proof route has a substantive mathematical gap.\\\",\\\"basis\\\":\\\"Task inputs frozen-target.md, problem.md, proof-draft.json, and source-context.md were read. The relevant NL0 v2 Yui rules for stage, format, self-containment, authoring, logical packaging, external/M source requirements, and templates were read. The draft's intended covering route was reviewed: its lower-bound interval-enlargement idea is logically plausible because each original projection B_i is contained in its enclosing interval J_i, so the enlarged-index family still covers every fiber; zero-diameter and scale-content details require explicit completion. No complete NL0 graph or Audit A review was created, and no acceptance is claimed. Source evidence must be obtained through successful pinned probes (or the source facts must be proved internally) before an artifact can responsibly be submitted.\\\",\\\"partial_progress\\\":\\\"Frozen target: for every n≥0 and nonempty compact E⊆Euclidean R^n, with I=[0,1] and the concatenated Euclidean metric on E×I, prove dim_H(E×I)=dim_H(E)+1; no extra hypotheses or definition properties were added. Candidate route retained: Hausdorff-cover subdivision for the upper bound; fiber covers, interval enlargements, and integration of the covering-cost inequality for the positive-dimension lower bound; nonempty-set coordinate projection for the zero-dimension lower bound. The pinned source file was located and read at Mathlib/Topology/MetricSpace/HausdorffDimension.lean, including the printed threshold-characterization declarations, but required probe evidence is unavailable. No structured spec/graph has been submitted, since a source-complete graph and evidence are not available.\\\"}\"}"}

